y 407 and 1468; 1495 receives only from 627, 1512, 1517, 1541. These sets are disjoint and the out-neighbourhoods of 407 and 1468 contain none of 1495's in-neighbours, so even ignoring time the shortest route is at least four hops. Given the near-one-shot edge regime (repeat ratio 0.034) and 695's total of six events, there is no evidence of a chain whose successive hops each fall within 600 time units inside the queried interval. High overall volume and 407's large out-degree explain apparent reachability without supporting a genuine time-respecting cascade."}, "raw_final_response": "**Conclusion**\n\nI used my full budget of 8 calls. Findings:\n\n- The graph is large but sparse in repeats (16,325 events, 15,767 distinct edges, repeat ratio 0.034) over a 100,000-unit horizon \u2014 events per node-pair are essentially one-off (step_01).\n- Source 695 is very low-activity: 6 events, 6 distinct partners, and only **two outgoing** partners: 407 and 1468 (step_02, step_03).\n- Target 1495 has 11 events and only **four incoming** partners: 627, 1512, 1517, 1541 (step_02, step_04).\n- The 1-hop out-set of 695 and the 1-hop in-set of 1495 are disjoint, so any influence chain needs \u22653 hops (step_05).\n- Neither 407 (59 out-partners) nor 1468 (14 out-partners) reaches any of 1495's in-neighbours (627/1512/1517/1541), so no 3-hop chain exists either; any static route is \u22654 hops (step_06, step_07) \u2014 this also serves as a confounder control: 407's large out-degree (\"popularity\") does not create a route into 1495.\n- The 2-hop neighbourhood of 1495 (step_08) is dominated by hub nodes (14, 45, 67, 70) that are not out-partners of 695, confirming the connection, if any, is long-range rather than a tight relay.\n\nA cascade requires every consecutive hop to follow within 600 time units. With a \u22654-hop static route, only one out-event from 695 per partner, and a near-one-shot edge regime, there is no supported chain of tightly spaced hops from 695 to 1495 inside [28025, 66424].\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_636b848d\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [695, 1495, 407, 1468, 627, 1512, 1517, 1541],\n  \"window\": [28025, 66424],\n  \"confidence\": 0.62,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"support\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"695 emits to only 407 and 1468; 1495 receives only from 627, 1512, 1517, 1541. These sets are disjoint and the out-neighbourhoods of 407 and 1468 contain none of 1495's in-neighbours, so even ignoring time the shortest route is at least four hops. Given the near-one-shot edge regime (repeat ratio 0.034) and 695's total of six events, there is no evidence of a chain whose successive hops each fall within 600 time units inside the queried interval. High overall volume and 407's large out-degree explain apparent reachability without supporting a genuine time-respecting cascade.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 24145, "total_output_tokens": 3756, "total_tokens": 27901, "total_latency_ms": 58049, "llm_calls": 6, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}